{{Term/Store|Pink Heron|Pink Herons|Series, BotW, TotK|plural}} are recurring [[Creature]]s in {{TLoZ Series}}.<ref>{{Cite|'''Pink Heron'''|Hyrule Compendium|BotW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|'''Pink Heron'''|Hyrule Compendium|TotK}}</ref>

==Characteristics==
==={{BotW|-}}===
{{Compendium/Extract|Pink Heron}}
Pink Herons are a large variety of [[Heron]] with long legs and an elongated neck, colored predominately white with pink wings and crest.<ref>{{Cite Book|quote= |book= CaC |publisher= |page= 164}}</ref> Meanwhile, their legs and beak are black. They often appear in flocks of two or more, strutting slowly about. If [[Link]] approaches them, they will fly away.<ref name="Compendium">{{Cite|This breed of heron is characterized by the pink tips of its feathers. Unlike its waterfront- dwelling relative the blue-winged heron, these live in grasslands or arid regions and subsist on insects that live in the grass. They can often be found walking about searching for food but will fly away if they sense danger.|Hyrule Compendium|BotW}}</ref> Unlike the [[Blue-Winged Heron]], these [[Bird]]s inhabit the grassy and arid [[Region]]s of [[Hyrule Ridge]] and [[Hyrule Field]], where they hunt [[Insect]]s.<ref name="Compendium"/>

When they are killed, Pink Herons will drop [[Raw Bird Drumstick]]s.

==={{TotK|-}}===
{{Compendium/Extract/TotK|Pink Heron}}
Pink Herons can be found near [[Dueling Peaks Stable]].

